nning trees \u2014 is a research-scale formalization. Passes 1\u20133 produced zero Lean across their budgets; pass 4 had $0.75 and used it to commit the algorithm and remove the hardest planned proof obligation (the fuel-based `find` termination block, ~250 lines, eliminated by the label-array design). It does not fit in a sub-dollar pass.\n\nTwo options for you, both your call rather than mine:\n- Give a substantially larger budget for a pass that writes Layers 0\u20135.\n- Descope the postcondition to `is_spanning_tree`, dropping optimality \u2014 roughly half the work, and Layers 0\u20134 land on a natural checkpoint.\n\nOne note on the plan I left in place: the algorithm never flips an edge's orientation, since `MSTEdge.is_valid` requires the pair to be stored in `adj[e.u]` and the adjacency array isn't assumed symmetric. A future pass should keep that."
